From: VUX9K
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: a queue of 4 requests of at most 8 KB

mmc's queue allocates all its requests when the card is found, each with a
scatterlist of the host's max_segs entries: 64 requests of 128 entries for
mmc_spi took a few hundred KB of unmovable slab, scattered over the 8 MB that
must keep contiguous blocks free for every exec (noMMU, FLAT), and the
largest free block fell below what busybox needs. 4 requests of at most 16
blocks (8 KB) are plenty for one polled SPI card. This tree's own patch, not
sent upstream (docs/agents/linux.md, "Kernel patches").

---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c b/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
index 5d187e0..10bb4c0 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/queue.c
@@ -418,8 +418,10 @@ static inline bool mmc_merge_capable(struct mmc_host *host)
 	return host->caps2 & MMC_CAP2_MERGE_CAPABLE;
 }
 
-/* Set queue depth to get a reasonable value for q->nr_requests */
-#define MMC_QUEUE_DEPTH 64
+/* Set queue depth to get a reasonable value for q->nr_requests. VUX9K: 4, as each
+ * request keeps its memory (a scatterlist) from the start, in 8 MB of RAM that also
+ * holds every running program as one contiguous block (noMMU, FLAT) */
+#define MMC_QUEUE_DEPTH 4
 
 /**
  * mmc_init_queue - initialise a queue structure.
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c b/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c
index 5217d71..e1a7168 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/mmc_spi.c
@@ -86,7 +86,9 @@
  * than 64 KBytes at a time. So use this value until there is any indication
  * that we should do more here.
  */
-#define MMC_SPI_BLOCKSATONCE	128
+/* VUX9K: 8 KB, so that each of the queue's requests keeps a scatterlist of 16
+ * entries, not 128; the polled port is slow per byte whatever the size */
+#define MMC_SPI_BLOCKSATONCE	16
 
 /****************************************************************************/
 
